---
# WORKFLOW of the kind certification (scripts/e2e_kind.sh + scripts/e2e/certify.py).
# `@VAR@` placeholders are filled by the scripts. The board is the memory tracker seeded from
# `tracker.issues`: every pod mounts this same file, so republishing it moves the ticket.
# There is no GitHub App and no Linear: the hook builds a local git repository.
tracker:
  kind: memory
  issues: @ISSUES@
polling:
  interval_ms: 5000
workspace:
  root: /workspace
hooks:
  after_create: |
    set -eu
    mkdir -p /workspace && cd /workspace
    git init -q -b main .
    git config user.name "Symphony E2E"
    git config user.email e2e@example.invalid
    printf '# kind e2e\n' > README.md
    git add README.md && git commit -q -m init
    # Never fetched: it records which repository this workspace is for, so the next
    # attempt reuses the workspace instead of treating it as another repository's.
    git remote add origin "${GITHUB_SERVER_URL:-https://github.com}/${SYMPHONY_TARGET_REPO}.git"
  before_run: |
    cd /workspace && git status --short
  timeout_ms: 60000
agent:
  max_concurrent_agents: 1
  max_turns: 1
  input_timeout_ms: 60000
engine:
  command: omp --mode rpc
  provider: "@PROVIDER@"
  model: "@MODEL@"
  thinking: low
  read_timeout_ms: 15000
kubernetes:
  agent_runtime: node
  agent_images:
    node: symphony-agent:node
  sandbox: {cpu: 1, memory_mib: 2048, timeout_s: 3600, idle_timeout_s: 1800}
  runner: {timeout_s: 1800, wallclock_guard_s: 1500}
  session_volume_size: 1Gi
  learning:
    enabled: false   # retrospectives open a learnings PR: they need the GitHub App
telemetry:
  enabled: true
---
You are working on ticket {{ issue.identifier }}: {{ issue.title }}

{{ issue.description }}

Work only inside /workspace, one shell command per step, and do not commit, push or call
linear_graphql. If a human message arrives while you work, do what it asks as well. When
everything is done, reply with a one-line summary.
